{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df874e2c-74b8-4c13-9865-4f79553e7814","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A string fixed at both ends can form a standing wave. These two curves show opposite extremes of one vibration pattern.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Standing waves on a string"},{"op":"figure","id":"string","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.4,6.4],"y":[-1.6,1.6],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"rest","from":[0,0],"to":[6,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"fn","id":"crest","y":"sin(pi*x/3)","domain":[0,6]},{"kind":"fn","id":"opposite","y":"-sin(pi*x/3)","domain":[0,6],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,-0.3],"to":[0,0.3]},{"kind":"segment","from":[6,-0.3],"to":[6,0.3]}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df874e2c-74b8-4c13-9865-4f79553e7814","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Nodes never move. Here, both fixed ends and the midpoint stay at zero displacement throughout the vibration.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"nodes","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"nodeleft","at":[0,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"nodemid","at":[3,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"noderight","at":[6,0],"label":"N"}]},{"op":"text","id":"nodedef","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Node: always zero displacement"}],"checkpoint":null}}
